*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]]\n*[[Cookbook:Noodle|Rice noodles]], cooked\n*Red [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] thin\n*[[Cookbook:Shallot|Shallots]], sliced thin\n\n==Procedure==\n#[[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] onion in olive oil until it is translucent.\n#Add chopped garlic.\n#Toss in placenta, and cook quickly.\n#Add a dash of fresh rosemary and the cumin.\n#Add a [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of salt and ground pepper to taste.\n#Serve on a bed of rice noodles, garnished with sliced red pepper and shallot.\n\n==Warnings==\n\n* As with any meat from uncontrolled sources (such as hunting or scavenging) people should be cautious of risks involved. Certain blood-borne diseases can live in blood and tissue outside the body for some time. Be sure that sensible precautions have been taken.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using placenta]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shallot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Spicy Placenta with Rice Noodles","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"2","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"250 grams of fresh human placenta, chopped into fine strips","sourceText":"250 grams of fresh human placenta, chopped into fine strips","amountText":"250 grams of fresh human placenta, chopped into fine strips","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 onion","sourceText":"1 onion","amountText":"1 onion","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 cloves of garlic, chopped","sourceText":"2 cloves of garlic, chopped","amountText":"2 cloves of garlic, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tablespoon of olive oil","sourceText":"1 tablespoon of olive oil","amountText":"1 tablespoon of olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":